<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 3</h2>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Helping Around the House</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> I Wash the Dishes Everyday.</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Describe favorite hobbies or activities briefly. Interactive: Exchange information about hobbies with peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can describe a favorite household chore or activity using simple sentences (e.g., "I like cooking with my mom." "My favorite chore is watering the plants."). Can have a simple discussion by asking and answering questions about chores and activities they do at home (e.g., "Do you help clean the house?" "Yes, I clean my room." "What chore do you like?" "I like doing the dishes."). Can explain how they do simple chores at home using basic sentences (e.g., "I sweep and mop the floor every day." "I wash the dishes and then dry them.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h3 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h3>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Stage & Description</h4></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; background-color: #f2f2f2;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Activities & Teacher Actions</h4></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Estimated Date and Time</h4></th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts with a "Chore Charades" activity. The teacher shows flashcards of household chores (e.g., a broom for "sweep the floor," hands washing dishes for "wash the dishes," a watering can for "water the plants," a cooking pot for "cook"). Students call out the name of the chore. The teacher then asks students, "What chores do you do at home?" and encourages simple answers like "I clean" or "I wash."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models sentences using the target vocabulary and grammar: "I wash the dishes every day." (emphasizing /w/ in 'wash'). "I sweep the floor often." (emphasizing /s/ in 'sweep'). "My mom cooks for the family." The teacher writes these on the board. The teacher points to a picture of someone cooking and says "cook" (closed syllable) and then "do" (open syllable), making students aware of the sound difference. Students repeat phrases chorally and individually, focusing on pronunciation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do I wash the dishes once a week or every day?" (Expected answer: "Every day.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'wash' a thing or an action?" (Expected answer: "An action.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Helping Around the House")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short dialogue between two friends, Maria and Carlos, discussing their daily chores at home, presented on a projected image or large flashcards with speech bubbles. The dialogue is simple and uses present simple tense, WH-questions, and frequency adverbs. Example: "Maria: What do you do at home, Carlos? Carlos: I help my mom cook every day. I also water the plants. What about you? Maria: I wash the dishes and clean my bedroom often."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Discussing routines: Describing daily tasks and house chores according to context.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Speaking-focused):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What are Maria and Carlos talking about?" (Expected answer: "House chores / Helping at home.") Students say their answers aloud.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Oral):</b> The teacher reads sentences based on the dialogue. Students say "True" or "False."
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Carlos washes the dishes." (False)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Maria cleans her bedroom." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Carlos cooks every day." (True)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Speaking)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice using the Present simple, WH-questions ("What do you do?", "How often do you...?"), and frequency adverbs ("every day," "often") with vocabulary such as: wash, clean, sweep, cook, help, dishes, floor, kitchen, bedroom, plants.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion (Oral):</b> The teacher displays incomplete sentences on the board or screen (e.g., "I ____ the dishes every day."). Students complete them orally, choosing from a set of target verbs (wash, clean, sweep, cook, water). The teacher ensures correct present simple form and pronunciation of /w/ and /s/.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-Controlled Practice - Substitution Drill (Choral/Individual):</b> The teacher leads a drill. Teacher says: "I wash the dishes." Students repeat. Teacher changes the object: "the clothes." Students say: "I wash the clothes." Teacher changes the verb: "clean the floor." Students say: "I clean the floor." This also includes varying frequency adverbs: "I clean my room often." "I clean my room every day."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Interaction - Q&A with Sentence Frames:</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher provides sentence frames on the board: "What chore do you ____ at home?" and "I ____ the ____ every day/often." or "Do you help ____ the ____?" and "Yes, I ____." Each student takes turns asking and answering questions about chores they do. The teacher circulates, providing feedback on accuracy and pronunciation, specifically the /w/ and /s/ sounds and differentiating between open and closed syllables in words like "do" and "cook".</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Helping Around the House")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative "Family Chore Interview" Role-Play.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups of 3-4. Each group creates a simple "family." One student is the "interviewer," and the others are "family members." The interviewer asks questions about chores using WH-questions and "Do you...?" forms. The "family members" describe their favorite household chore or activity and how often they do it, using target vocabulary (e.g., wash, clean, sweep, cook, organize, dishes, floor, kitchen, bedroom, laundry, plants) and frequency adverbs (every day, often, usually).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example interactions:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A (Interviewer): "What do you do in the kitchen?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B (Family Member): "I wash the dishes and wipe the table every day."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "Do you help clean the living room?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student C (Family Member): "Yes, I sweep the floor often and dust the furniture."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "What chore do you like?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student D (Family Member): "I like watering the plants."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher monitors groups, offering support for fluency, correct grammar, and encouraging natural interaction.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the "Family Chore Interview" role-play.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform their "Family Chore Interview" role-play in front of another group or the class.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Speaking focus):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of target words (e.g., /w/ in "wash", /s/ in "sweep").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., dishes, sweep, clean, cook).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of present simple tense.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to ask and answer simple WH-questions and "Do you...?" questions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and clear communication within the group.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an oral exit ticket by sharing one sentence: "One chore I do at home is _____. I do it _____." (e.g., "I wash the dishes. I do it every day.")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy to talk about today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was difficult to say in English?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The "Family Chore Interview" activity worked well to promote fluent speaking and interaction, especially with the use of sentence frames. Most students confidently used the present simple and common chore vocabulary. Some students still needed prompting for correct WH-question formation and consistent use of frequency adverbs. I noticed some difficulty with the 'th' sound in 'the' for some students, which I will scaffold more. I also need to reinforce the distinction between open and closed syllables with more examples in future lessons. Group dynamics were positive, and students enjoyed sharing about their home tasks.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Next Lesson:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This speaking practice will prepare students for Lesson 4 (Writing Composition), where they will write short paragraphs describing their own household chores and routines, building on the vocabulary and grammatical structures practiced today. They will use the sentences they orally produced today to construct written descriptions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>